+# Definition of Done
+
+> The orchestrator's `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error`. A rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string, a plain object, a value from a library that rejects with its own shape — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
+
+**Strategy: `direct`** — the seam already exists. `createChatOrchestrator` accepts `options.hooks.onError` and drives the turn through `processMessage`, so the acceptance test can exercise string, plain-object, and `undefined` rejections directly against the real orchestrator entry point today and observe `onError` being skipped while the original rejection propagates to the caller.
+
+## Done when these pass
+
+- [ ] **wraps a non-Error rejection in an Error whose cause is the original and still rejects the caller with the original** — rejects a provider turn with a string, a plain object, and `undefined`, asserting for each that `onError` is called once with the session and an `Error` instance carrying the thrown value on its own `cause` property while `processMessage` still rejects with the original value unchanged
+  `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts`
+
+## Facets
+
+- [ ] In `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts`, remove the `error instanceof Error` gate on `hooks.onError`: pass an `Error` rejection to `onError` as the same instance, wrap any non-`Error` rejection in `new Error(String(error), {cause: error})` (preserving `cause` even when `undefined`), and keep `throw error` re-throwing the original rejection value unchanged at the caller boundary.
+- [ ] Keep existing `onError` tests in `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts` unedited and green so `Error` rejections continue reaching `onError` unwrapped.
+- [ ] Add an entry under `## [Unreleased]` in `CHANGELOG.md` describing what changes for an existing consumer (`onError` now fires for non-`Error` rejections wrapped with `{cause}`, while the caller-boundary rejection value stays unchanged).
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- `beforeSession` escaping the `try` (HALEngine#94, already shipped).
+- Usage accounting across tool rounds (HALEngine#93, already shipped).
